{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "action" %}
{# SeverActions - Book Reading Mode. Uses StorageUtil via papyrus_util.
   GATE ON LINE 1: SkyrimNet's best-practices lint requires the render_mode
   {% if %} within the FIRST 5 LINES (PromptEngine warns + flags the prompt
   as a response-delay risk otherwise) - comments go BELOW the gate.
   Dialogue/thoughts renders stay CLEAN for non-readers. The idle "don't
   recite from memory" rule renders ONLY in the action pass (render_mode
   "action") as a warm-up right where ReadBook gets chosen - plus the
   readbook.yaml description and the execute-time DirectNarration. Full
   rules + book text still land via states 1/2 the moment the action fires. #}
{% set isReading = papyrus_util("GetIntValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBook", 0) %}
{% if render_mode == "action" and isReading == 0 %}
**Book Reading Rule (if choosing ReadBook):** You do not know what any book says — its real text appears in context only AFTER the ReadBook action fires. Never recite, quote, or invent book contents from memory; roleplay opening the book and let the text arrive.
{% endif %}
{% if isReading == 1 %}
{% set bookTitle = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookTitle", "") %}
{% set bookText = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookText", "") %}
{% if bookText != "" %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
## BOOK READING MODE — ACTIVE

{{ actor.name }} has opened "{{ bookTitle }}" and must now read it aloud.

The book's complete text is between the markers below. Nothing you remember about this book from elsewhere applies.

===BEGIN BOOK TEXT===
{{ bookText }}
===END BOOK TEXT===

**Reading rules:**
1. Read ONLY the exact text between the markers, word for word — never invent, add, or recall content from memory. Do not paraphrase or embellish.
2. Read continuously — as much of the text as possible per response. Ignore any dialogue length limits.
3. Do not repeat text already read; pick up where you left off. No title between sections, no commentary, no narrated actions (no clearing throats or turning pages), no closing remarks when stopping mid-text.
4. When you have read every word, use **StopReading** — the ONLY action available in reading mode. Only after it may you share thoughts in character; do not use ReadBook again.

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if isReading == 2 %}
{% set bookTitle = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookTitle", "") %}
{% set bookText = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookText", "") %}
{% if bookText != "" %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
## BOOK READING MODE — SUMMARIZE & REACT

{{ actor.name }} has read "{{ bookTitle }}" and must now summarize it and share their thoughts.

The book's complete text is between the markers below. Nothing you remember about this book from elsewhere applies.

===BEGIN BOOK TEXT===
{{ bookText }}
===END BOOK TEXT===

**SUMMARY RULES — YOU MUST FOLLOW ALL OF THESE:**
1. You have read the entire book above. Now summarize it in your own words, IN CHARACTER as {{ actor.name }}.
2. Give a concise summary of the book's contents — cover the key points, themes, or story.
3. After the summary, share {{ actor.name }}'s personal thoughts, opinions, and reactions. How does this book relate to their experiences? Do they agree or disagree with its ideas? Does it remind them of anything?
4. You may reference or briefly quote short passages you found especially interesting, but do NOT recite the full text.
5. Do NOT invent content that is not in the book text above. Only summarize and react to what is actually written.
6. Speak naturally in character. This is a conversation, not a book report.
7. You are unrestricted on response length — take the space a thorough summary and genuine reaction need.
8. When you are done sharing your thoughts, use **StopReading** — the ONLY action available in reading mode.

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
